<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33721" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλῑνύω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.67
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Hp.
			<u>Acut.</u>
			47
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Pr.</u>
			53
		</span></i>: impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλίνυον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.71
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠλ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Mith.</u>
					43
				</span></i>
			; 
				Ion.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλινύεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.589
				</span></i>
			: fut.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ύσω [ῡ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
			</span></i>&lt;*&gt;.<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				2.46
			</span></i>: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλίνῡσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.56
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				529
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.:—Poet. and 
				Ion.
			 Verb, also used in Trag. and late Prose (as <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Num.</u>
				14
			</span></i>), <i>keep holiday, take rest, repose</i>, freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i>, as <i><span class="en">
				<u>Acut.</u>
				47
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ἐλινύειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.67
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διέβη ὁ στρατὸς . . ἐλινύσας
				οὐδένα χρόνον</span> without any <i>cessation</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.56
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλινύσοντα . . ἀγάλματα</span>
			<i>to stand unmoved</i> on their pedestals, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				5.1
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>I.</u>
				2.46
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς μή σ᾽ ἐλινύοντα προσδερχθῇ
				πατήρ</span> see thee <i>standing idle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				53
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἐλινύειν ἐχρῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					598
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. μίαν ἡμέραν</span> Orac.
				ap.<i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.53
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. gen. rei,
				<i>rest from</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλήθεος βρώμης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Acut.</u>
					47
				</span></i>
			 (v.l.&lt;<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ&gt;</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; ἔργων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.33
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c.
			part., <i>rest</i> or <i>cease from</i> doing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλίνυον οὐδένα χρόνον . . ἐργαζόμενοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.71
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				529
			</span></i>(lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Cer.</u>
				48
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				248
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υ</span> of the impf.
			short in <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.862
			</span></i>, long ib.<i><span class="en">
				589
			</span></i>, indeterminate in Trag.] (Written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλιννύω</span> in some codd.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
